Yang,

a) *never* set JAVA_HOME - it is likely to break things. Simply make sure "java" on the command line works before you run R CMD javareconf
b) to get config.log, unpack the tar ball and install using R CMD INSTALL rJava -- the config.log will be in the rJava directory

If you have issues, please post the full result of javareconf and possibly the config.log.

Cheers,
Simon



